    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 0a094208431f6d0778848fa06842597fe45c8ed9 -->\n**Delta review of the merge of main (0a094208), standing on the full review of 44af57e4 (re-read; it had no code blockers). Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\n`cargo xtask merge-plan --delta` reported DELTA (hand-resolved), so I read `git show --remerge-diff` and rebuilt.\n\n**Resolution checked:**\n- Both sides kept in all 13 hand-resolved files (`kinds.rs`, `types/params.rs`, `types/mod.rs`, `generate.rs`, `posting.rs`, `setup_sheet/heights.rs`, `create.rs`, `edit.rs`, `stamp.rs`, and the count pins in `operation/tests.rs`, `ribbon.rs`, `coarse_laws.rs`, `lathe_voice_tests.rs`). `WireContour` arms are all still present next to the `SinkerBurn`/`SinkerSideBurn` arms.\n- Ordinals and tags: WireContour 41, SinkerBurn 42, SinkerSideBurn 43. `KindInfo` tag 43 and `ALL_LABELS` have the new entry; nothing existing moved. The `KindInfo::ALL.len()` pin is 44 and the lathe-voice pin is (12, 1, 31).\n- `create.rs` imports and `edit.rs` `ChangeOperationKind` still run `family_gate`, `sinker_gate`, `tool_door`, `wire_gate`; no refusal dropped.\n- `stamp.rs`: the side-gap term is still in the digest. The tool terms (centre-cutting, body, cutter) the PR side had inline are gone from `stamp.rs` because main moved them into `stamp_tool::write` (called at `stamp.rs:45`), so they are neither lost nor doubled.\n\n**Local results at 0a094208:**\n- `camcraft-app --lib`: 154 passed.\n- App suites: `sinker_side` 5, `sinker_burn` 9, `sinker_orbit` 6, `wire_contour` 7, `tool_law` 4, `coarse_laws` 6, `ribbon` 12, all passed.\n- `camcraft-ui --lib ribbon` (CWD `crates/ui`): 12 passed.\n- Clippy `-D warnings` on `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui` (all targets): clean.\n\n**Requested before merge:** none.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
